<<
/A 1931 0 R
/Alt (Illustration shows PDNVs trafficking within a cell, highlighting movement from the nucleus through the endoplasmic reticulum to endosomes, with diagrams detailing vesicle cargo such as nucleic acids, proteins, and lipids. Insets categorize nucleic acids \(DNA, mRNA, miRNA, RNA fragments\), proteins \(HSP, aquaporins, RNA-BP, annexins, actin, transport proteins, enzymes\), and lipids \(PA, PC, PE, SM, GSL\). Key vesicle surface features include surface antigens, adhesion molecules, tetraspanins, and lipid rafts, with cargo labeled as nucleic acids, proteins, and lipids.)
